The <ansi fg="command">mob</ansi> command can be used in the following ways:

<ansi fg="command">mob spawn loot goblin</ansi>
A special case mob spawn command that puts the loot goblin into play.

<ansi fg="command">mob spawn [name/MobId]</ansi>
    <ansi fg="command">mob spawn [MobId]</ansi> - e.g. <ansi fg="command">mob spawn 1</ansi>
    <ansi fg="command">mob spawn [MobName]</ansi> - e.g. <ansi fg="command">mob spawn goblin</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">mob list</ansi>
List all mob names.

<ansi fg="command">mob list [name-to-search]</ansi>
List mobs that match a provided search term. You can use a wildcard on either
or both sides of the search term, such as <ansi fg="command">mob list *frost*</ansi>.

<ansi fg="command">mob heal [instId]</ansi>
Restore a mob's Health, Stamina, and Conviction to their max values.
Useful for sustained combat testing (e.g., observing per-round grapple
mechanics, weapon-reach narration) against a target that would normally
die in a few rounds.
    <ansi fg="command">mob heal 12</ansi>    Heal a specific mob instance.
    <ansi fg="command">mob heal</ansi>       (no id) Heal every mob in the current room.

